{title: Lord of the Dance}
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_verse: 1}
I [C]danced in the [Am]morning when the [Em]world was be[Am]gun
And I [Dm]danced in the [**]moon and the [**]stars and the [G]sun
And I [C]came down from [Am]heaven and I [Em]danced on the [Am]earth
At [Dm]Bethle[G]hem I [F]had my [C]birth.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[C]Dance, [Em]then, wher[**]ever you may [Am]be
[C]I am the [**]Lord of the [Dm]dance, said [G]he
And I'll [C]lead you [F]all, wher[C]ever you may be[C]
And I'll [F]lead you [G]all in the [C]dance, said h[C]e.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
I [C]danced for the [Am]scribe and the [Em]Phari[Am]see
But they [Dm]would not [**]dance and they [**]wouldn't follow [G]me
I [C]danced for the [Am]fishermen, for [Em]James and [Am]John
They [Dm]came with [G]me and the [F]dance went [C]on:
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: 3}
I [C]danced on the [Am]Sabbath and I [Em]cured the [Am]lame
The [Dm]holy [**]people said [**]it was a [G]shame
They [C]whipped and they [Am]stripped and they [Em]hung me on [Am]high
And they [Dm]left me [G]there on a [F]cross to [C]die:
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: 4}
I [C]danced on a [Am]Friday when the [Em]sky turned [Am]black
It's [Dm]hard to [**]dance with the [**]devil on your [G]back
They [C]buried my [Am]body and they [Em]thought I'd [Am]gone
But [Dm]I am the [G]dance, and I [F]still go [C]on:
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: 5}
They [C]cut me [Am]down and [Em]I leapt up [Am]high
I [Dm]am the [**]life that'll [**]never, never [G]die
I'll [C]live in [Am]you if you'll [Em]live in [Am]me
I [Dm]am the [G]Lord of the [F]dance, said [C]he.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
